Task 12: Extended Metro Fare System
1. Airport Zone
An Airport Zone is added with a base fare of ₹60. The fare table must support the additional zone.
2. Weekend Discount
A 10% discount is applied to eligible weekend journeys. The weekend discount cannot be combined with the peak surcharge. Therefore, weekend journeys receive the discount instead of the peak surcharge.
3. Monthly Pass
A monthly pass allows unlimited journeys within two selected zones. The system checks whether the journey's zone is included in the pass before charging the normal fare.
4. Validation
The system validates the zone, time, balance, and selected pass zones. Money is stored in integer paise to avoid floating-point rounding errors.
5. Conclusion
The extended system supports airport travel, weekend discounts, and monthly passes while maintaining fare accuracy and minimum-balance validation for journeys charged a fare.
